  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIWI Building Governance Capacity for Improved Water Security (GO-WATER)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SIWI Building Governance Capacity for improved Water Security (GO-WATER)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Stockholms International Water Institute (SIWI) har inkommit med f&#xf6;rslag p&#xe5; ett kapacitetsutvecklingsprogram inom vattenf&#xf6;rvaltning i Afghanistan, Irak, Sudan, samt Bolivia, Peru och Colombia under ben&#xe4;mning &quot;Building Governance Capacity for improved Water Security (GOWATER)&quot; och som ska genomf&#xf6;ras med lokala 
samarbetspartners. SIWI har l&#xe5;ng erfarenhet av arbete inom detta omr&#xe5;de och erh&#xe5;llit st&#xf6;d under l&#xe5;ng tid av Sida f&#xf6;r olika initiativ som denna insats kommer att komplettera. SIWI &#xe4;r en stiftelse vars syfte &#xe4;r att fr&#xe4;mja forskning och utveckling kring vatten genom att bedriva internationellt inriktad forsknings- och utvecklingsverksamhet. SIWI&apos;s vision &#xe4;r en &quot; water wise world&quot; med missionen
&quot;SIWl provides and promotes water wise solutions for sustainable development&quot;. Detta inneb&#xe4;r att SIWI bidrar till generering och spridning av ny kunskap, utbildning och p&#xe5;verkansarbete for h&#xe5;llbara beslut och h&#xe5;llbar hantering av vatten.

Programmet har fokus p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka institutionell kapacitet f&#xf6;r vatten- och sanitetsf&#xf6;rvaltning i de deltagande l&#xe4;nderna  och ska d&#xe4;rmed skapa f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningar f&#xf6;r att bygga effektivare vatten- och sanitetsf&#xf6;rvaltning f&#xf6;r att bidra till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad vattens&#xe4;kerhet och vattenresiliens f&#xf6;r fattiga kvinnor, m&#xe4;n, flickor och pojkar. En f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad vattens&#xe4;kerhet och vattenresiliens antas ocks&#xe5; leda till j&#xe4;mlikare samh&#xe4;llen. Det handlar konkret om f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad styrning och f&#xf6;rvaltning f&#xf6;r att leverera rent vatten och sanitet till fattiga m&#xe4;nniskor p&#xe5; ett h&#xe5;llbart s&#xe4;tt och med regelbundenhet &#xf6;ver tid. F&#xf6;r detta kr&#xe4;vs bland annat l&#xe4;rande och erfarenhetsutbyte mellan akt&#xf6;rer i vatten- och sanitetssektorn i de deltagande l&#xe4;nderna f&#xf6;r att bygga p&#xe5;, och accelerera, redan identifierade reformprocesser i vatten- och sanitetssektorn.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme is focussing on developing capacities for improved water and sanitary governance in the participating countries (Afghanistan, Iraq and Sudan &amp; Bolivia, Colombia and Peru). The programme will hence contribute to build more effective water and sanitary governance contributing to enhanced water security and resilience for poor women, men, girls and boys. Enhanced water security and water resilience may also be conducive to more equal societies. It is about concrete and improved governance to deliver pure water and sanitary solutions to poor people sustainably and regularly. This requires learning and peer-to-peer exchange between stakeholders in the water and sanitary sector of the participating countries. This to reinforce and accelerate already identified reform processes in the water and sanitary sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">&#xd6;vergripande m&#xe5;l: &apos;To build more effective water sector institutions, contributing to improved water security and resilience for poverty eradication and social equity.&apos;
Delm&#xe5;l 1: &apos;Building vision and further commitment on water policy implementation and improved operational efficiency for selected key water institutions to deliver on their institutional mandate.&apos;
Outcome 1: &apos;Selected key water institutions with improved capacity to implement their mandate to manage water resources and/or deliver water and sanitation services in efficient, equitable and sustainable ways.&apos;
Sub-outcome 1.1: &apos;Water sector institutions are enabled to develop and implement governance measures that improve their operational efficiency.&apos;
Sub-outcome 1.2:&#xa0;&apos;Water Reform Working Group Projects for improved governance developed and ready for uptake by selected key water institution.&apos;
Delm&#xe5;l 2: &apos;Building water governance knowledge and regional exchange.&apos;
Outcome 2: &apos;Water governance knowledge advanced, incorporated into easily accessible knowledge management tools and shared and discussed for mutual peer-to-peer learning between countries.&apos;
Sub-outcome 2.1: &apos;Knowledge and research on water governance generated from country experiences.&apos;
Sub-outcome 2.2:&#xa0;&apos;In-country knowledge and experiences shared among water stakeholders at multi-country workshops.&apos;</narrative>
  </description>
